{"author_association":"OWNER","body":"## Independent PM review — G4 decision (2026-11-01)\n\n**Decision: APPROVE G4 for the bounded M7 Option B evaluation evidence (M7-01 through M7-03), with explicit scientific limitations.** Reviewed PR #17 at HEAD `5907ab6a79494a367aed011919d36ac80f5d3164` against `docs/06-quality/ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md`, the frozen protocol, campaign/analysis reports, the evidence and test provenance, and the relevant application/test implementation. This is an **independent PM gate decision**, not executor self-approval or a claim of improved chess performance.\n\n### Acceptance findings\n1. **M7-01 — ACCEPT (bounded).** The predeclared nine-policy population (M4 behavior-only, six M5 post-RL checkpoints, RandomLegal, SimpleHeuristic) was evaluated on the stated ALE/VideoChess configuration against the approved built-in opponent. All 90/90 scheduled cells had observed resets. Results remain **60 terminal White losses and 30 incomplete attempts, zero wins or draws**. The baseline/pretraining/post-RL comparisons are descriptive only; the single ALE opponent, White-only control, small sample and incomplete outcomes do not establish superiority, equivalence, transfer or generalization.\n2. **M7-02 — ACCEPT.** The ten common ALE seeds, policy/training seed identities, player color, deterministic scheduling, resource limits/accounting, hash-linked provenance, raw metrics, censoring, deviations, and verification/failure history are recorded. Results are reconciled in the committed machine-readable analysis. Incomplete attempts are **not** classified as wins, losses, draws or terminal ties. One policy has zero terminal games and therefore an undefined terminal-only score. Only 9/30 Warm/Scratch matched pairs have terminal observations; the paired interval is correctly **unavailable**.\n3. **M7-03 — ACCEPT as non-reportability.** **No Elo number** is issued. The necessary calibrated opponent pool, rating anchor, color-balanced design and uncertainty method are not approved/available, so inventing an Elo or 1500-Elo assertion would violate the criterion.\n\n### Verification and boundaries\n- Examined application/protocol/analysis and relevant tests; full local run evidence records **492 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed**. The final GitHub preflight passed at exactly this PR HEAD; this CI check is **not** a substitute for the full suite.\n- Raw ROM, checkpoints, traces and campaign artifacts remain private/owner-local. PM verified the committed audit trail, code, hashes and internal consistency **but did not independently access and rerun the owner-local raw files**; this distinction remains in the handover. No private artifacts are approved for publication.\n- Observed outcome does **not** establish strong or successful chess play. O-02 (whether actual full-game performance is a hard academic requirement) remains an unresolved owner/instructor question, not a scientifically proven pass. All course-performance/publication claims must disclose this limitation.\n- Existing M4, M5, M6 v1/v2 and M7 tracks remain distinct; no retroactive edits or cross-track pooling are accepted. G3 remains approved; **G5 is NOT APPROVED**.\n- This PM decision approves the G4 *evaluation evidence* only. It is **not** approval to publish, release, allocate new compute, repeat/extend the campaign, or change frozen data/results.\n\n### Required canonical handoff before M7-004/005\nThe PR deliberately still records G4 as HOLD. After this PR merges, the executor must record this **actual independent PM decision**, with its PR/comment reference and merge commit, in canonical governance state and the appropriate gate evidence, preserving the decision boundaries. That update requires its own normal review/integration. **Do not start M7-004 or M7-005 until canonical G4 approval is integrated and verified.** M7-004 deliverables then require separate G5 review; M7-005/publication additionally requires explicit owner permission.\n\n**PM disposition: approve this Phase I PR for merge at its audited HEAD; authorize only the narrow G4-governance-record update as the next step, not the gated delivery work.**","created_at":"2026-11-01T02:54:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/dodaonam/atari-videochess-rl/pull/17#issuecomment-6552570969","id":6552570969,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dodaonam/atari-videochess-rl/issues/comments/6552570969","user":"dodaonam"}
